      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "42b13fa9-f779-52c5-995b-08a8b2b86711",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Thomas Fitch, Doc Holliday, Virgil Earp, Morgan Earp, Wyatt Earp, Billy Clanton, Tom McLaury, Frank McLaury\n- Events: Gunfight at the O.K. Corral\n- Roles: lawyer, gambler, gunfighter, dentist\n\nFacts:\n- On October 25, 1881, the Gunfight at the O.K. Corral was identified in this chunk as the event during which Billy Clanton, Tom McLaury, and Frank McLaury were killed.\n- After the October 25, 1881 Gunfight at the O.K. Corral, Thomas Fitch successfully defended Virgil Earp, Morgan Earp, Wyatt Earp, and Doc Holliday against accusations that they had murdered Billy Clanton, Tom McLaury, and Frank McLaury.\n- John Henry \"Doc\" Holliday was born on August 14, 1851, and died on November 8, 1887.\n- Doc Holliday was an American gambler, gunfighter, and dentist.\n- Doc Holliday was a good friend of Wyatt Earp.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
